# Screen toys: animations and effects, one stanza per program.  The
# play-tests in tools/playtests cover bite, card, life, rain and
# worms.

shot    ttyexp
size    30 80
cap     Fireworks for a terminal: bursts of characters are thrown out
cap     from a point, arc under gravity and fall away, with trails.  Each
cap     option is one letter and a number: -s how many bursts at once,
cap     -p how many points in each, -x and -y the size, -w a wind, -D how
cap     many seconds it runs.  It clears the screen when it is done.
try     ttyexp -s2 -p50
run     ttyexp -s2 -p50
wait    3
snap
wait    2
snap
wait    7

shot    xmas
size    24 80
cap     A Christmas card drawn in characters: the tree is drawn and trimmed,
cap     lights blink along its strings, and reindeer run across the screen
cap     before the card starts over.  It loops until control-C.
try     xmas
run     xmas
wait    60
snap
send    \003
wait    2

shot    rot22
size    24 80
cap     Software rot, demonstrated: the letters of a file come loose a few at
cap     a time and fall down the screen, piling up at the bottom until the
cap     text has drained out of the top.  Give it a file or pipe text in.
cap     This is a still from partway through; it is a moving picture.
try     rot22 DOC/README-CIO
run     builtin cd /dd
wait    1
run     clear
wait    1
run     rot22 DOC/README-CIO
wait    3
snap
wait    12
